  "gold_standard_summary": "## Patient Summary — James Okafor (DOB: 1963-04-14, Male, Age 62)\n\n**⚠️ INTOLERANCE: ACE inhibitors (class) — persistent dry cough. Do NOT prescribe any ACE inhibitor; patient is on sacubitril/valsartan (ARNI) as alternative.**\n\n**⚠️ CRITICAL MEDICATION NOTE: Clopidogrel (dual antiplatelet therapy) — post-DES stent Aug 2025. Do NOT discontinue without cardiology approval (minimum 12-month course).**\n\n**Active Conditions:** CHF with reduced EF (EF 35%); NSTEMI (Aug 2025) with DES stent to LAD; Coronary artery disease; Hypertension; Hyperlipidemia; Type 2 diabetes.\n\n**Medications (Guideline-Directed Medical Therapy):**\n- Aspirin 81mg + Clopidogrel 75mg (dual antiplatelet — post-stent)\n- Sacubitril/Valsartan 49/51mg BID (ARNI — HFrEF)\n- Carvedilol 25mg BID (beta-blocker)\n- Furosemide 40mg + Spironolactone 25mg (diuresis + aldosterone blockade)\n- Atorvastatin 80mg (high-intensity post-ACS)\n- Dapagliflozin 10mg (SGLT2i — HFrEF benefit)\n- Metformin 1000mg BID\n\n**Key Labs (Nov 2025):** BNP 310 pg/mL (down from 820 on admission — improving). LDL 62 mg/dL (target met). Potassium 4.8 mEq/L (borderline — monitor on spironolactone + ARNI). eGFR 56. HbA1c 7.4%.\n\n**Vitals:** BP 118/72 mmHg, HR 58 bpm, O2 sat 97%, weight 198 lbs (down 6 lbs — fluid improving).\n\n**Recent Procedures:** PCI with DES to LAD (Aug 12, 2025); Echo EF 35%; Cardiac cath (LAD 90%); Cardiac rehab 28 sessions completed.\n\n**Clinical Impression:** Post-NSTEMI stabilization on full GDMT. BNP trending down. LDL at target. Hyperkalemia risk — monitor K+ closely on spironolactone + ARNI. ACE inhibitor class contraindicated (cough intolerance). Do not interrupt dual antiplatelet therapy.\n\n---\n⚠️ DRAFT — AI-GENERATED — REQUIRES CLINICIAN REVIEW",
